From ee585d75ff46471b128fc4e129df05c98e0b61e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lorenzo Giannoccaro <giannoccarol@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 17:33:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] liboverlay: use the kernel value of MDP_Y_CBCR_H2V2_VENUS

The fallback that defined MDP_Y_CBCR_H2V2_VENUS as MDP_IMGTYPE_LIMIT when
VENUS_COLOR_FORMAT is missing shadowed the enum of the kernel msm_mdp.h.
The MDP rejected every Venus NV12 buffer with 'invalid pipe format 47' and
'invalid rot format 47', so hardware video and the camera preview fell back
to GPU composition.
---
 liboverlay/overlayUtils.h | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/liboverlay/overlayUtils.h b/liboverlay/overlayUtils.h
index 5e3bd1f..8b7aa2f 100644
--- a/liboverlay/overlayUtils.h
+++ b/liboverlay/overlayUtils.h
@@ -45,10 +45,10 @@
 #include <utils/Log.h>
 #include "gralloc_priv.h" //for interlace
 
-// Older platforms do not support Venus
-#ifndef VENUS_COLOR_FORMAT
-#define MDP_Y_CBCR_H2V2_VENUS MDP_IMGTYPE_LIMIT
-#endif
+// MDP_Y_CBCR_H2V2_VENUS comes from the kernel's msm_mdp.h (27 on msm8994).
+// The old fallback to MDP_IMGTYPE_LIMIT, taken whenever msm_media_info.h is
+// missing, shadowed it: the MDP rejected every Venus NV12 buffer ("invalid
+// pipe/rot format 47") and video was composed by the GPU.
 
 /*
 *
